        "original_id": "45e50ac4-e59e-5506-a9c6-c6ee7d675d5c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Pop Will Eat Itself, Black Stone Cherry\n- Places: Edmonton, Kentucky\n- Music releases: studio albums, EPs, singles, Kentucky\n\nFacts:\n- Pop Will Eat Itself initially disbanded in 1996.\n- Black Stone Cherry formed in 2001 in Edmonton, Kentucky.\n- Pop Will Eat Itself briefly reformed in 2005.\n- Black Stone Cherry released the studio albums \"Black Stone Cherry\" in 2006 and \"Folklore and Superstition\" in 2008.\n- Pop Will Eat Itself issued its first release in more than five years in 2010.\n- Black Stone Cherry released \"Between the Devil and the Deep Blue Sea\" in 2011 and \"Magic Mountain\" in 2014.\n- Black Stone Cherry released its fifth album, \"Kentucky,\" on April 1, 2016.\n- Black Stone Cherry has released three EPs and charted eight singles on the US Mainstream Rock Tracks charts.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a62a84c4-0a4f-5c64-80ae-da9415324eb1",
        "text": "Page: Pop Will Eat Itself. Sentence: After initially disbanding in 1996, and having a brief reformation in 2005, they issued their first release in more than five years in 2010.\nPage: Black Stone Cherry. Sentence: Black Stone Cherry is an American hard rock band, formed in 2001 in Edmonton, Kentucky.\nPage: Black Stone Cherry. Sentence: Black Stone Cherry has released five studio albums: \"Black Stone Cherry\" (2006), \"Folklore and Superstition\" (2008), \"Between the Devil and the Deep Blue Sea\" (2011), \"Magic Mountain\" (2014), and \"Kentucky\" (2016), as well as three EPs, and have charted eight singles on the US Mainstream Rock Tracks charts.\nPage: Black Stone Cherry. Sentence: The band's fifth album, \"Kentucky\" was released on April 1, 2016.",
